    - rid: 8910043418339312165
      type: {class: 'Constant`1[[System.String, mscorlib]]', ns: Unity.GraphToolkit.Editor, asm: Unity.GraphToolkit.Internal.Editor}
      data:
        m_Value: It was salt, the one common denominator that tied all the infected
          cases together. We missed it in so many tests under the belief that they
          were simply dying of heart failure. The tissue was retaining far too much
          water, their hands and feet were bloated but we assumed it was a byproduct
          of the sickness.\n\n  Sodium levels were abnormally elevated, they were
          being actively dehydrated at a rapid rate. Administering fluids seems to
          slow the spread down, but it does not stop it. The rate is slow enough
          that they can survive after,
    - rid: 8910043418339312166
      type: {class: DefaultPage, ns: BookGraph.Editor, asm: Assembly-CSharp-Editor}
      data: 
